course: dictionary
lesson: 12078
title: Clipped: one word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one to use. Clipped is a good example. It is the past form of the verb clip, so it can mean cut short, fastened, or touched lightly. Read the words around it to decide which meaning fits.
explain: «Grandma clipped the roses in the garden.» Roses are cut short and neat, so clipped means cut here. «Mia clipped the badge onto her coat.» A badge is pinned on with a clip, so clipped means fastened.
explain: Clipped can also describe a way of speaking. «"Leave now," he said in a clipped voice.» A clipped voice is short, quick and rather unfriendly. The words are few and sharp, so he is probably cross or in a hurry.
fact: Clip is a verb, and clipped is its past form: clip, clips, clipped, clipping.
fact: «Clipped» can mean cut short or neat, as with hair, nails or a hedge.
fact: «Clipped» can mean fastened with a clip, as with papers or a badge.
fact: «Clipped» can mean hit something lightly or quickly on the edge: a car that clipped a kerb just touched it.
fact: A clipped voice or answer is short, quick and rather unfriendly. Check the sentence to see which meaning fits.
exercise: «Grandma clipped the roses in the garden.» What does clipped mean here? | *Cut short and neat | Fastened together with a clip | Spoken in a loud voice | Hit very hard
exercise: «Ben clipped the photos together with a red clip.» What does clipped mean here? | *Fastened with a clip | Painted bright red | Cut short and neat | Dropped on the floor
exercise: «"No. Go away," he said in a clipped voice.» What kind of voice is it? | Soft, like a whisper in the dark | *Short, quick and rather unfriendly | Long, gentle and kind | Loud, happy and full of laughter
test: «The car clipped the kerb as it turned.» What does clipped mean here? | Painted bright red | *Touched lightly on the edge | Stopped completely | Driven away very fast
test: Which word is the past form of the verb clip? | clips | clip | clipping | *clipped
exam: «Her clipped answer showed she was in a hurry.» What does clipped mean in this sentence? | Long and cheerful | *Short, quick and rather unfriendly | Written in ink | Covered in mud
